# Line endings.
#
# Tests and guards match exact source text, and the vendored Bevy sources are compared with the
# published crates, so a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` must not turn them into CRLF.
# The later rules win: vendored files detect their own type, and every Rust, WGSL and TOML file
# (and `Cargo.lock`) is always LF. The guards also normalise CRLF when they read a source
# (`crates/engine/src/bevy_source.rs`), so a checkout made before this file is safe too.
vendor/** text=auto eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.wgsl text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
